================================================================================
SLIDE 1: PROBLEM OVERVIEW & APPROACH SUMMARY
================================================================================
* Business Problem: Predict physician adoption of Drug XYZ to prioritize sales force efforts for Q11.
* Objective: Build an end-to-end, leakage-free predictive pipeline and identify the top 200 high-priority target physicians out of 1,502 test candidates.
* Target Definition: Binary adoption flag (1 if total historical rx_count > 0 across Q1–Q10, else 0).
* Approach Overview: Merged longitudinal quarterly engagement data with static HCP profile data, engineered dynamic behavior metrics, performed strict leakage-free preprocessing, evaluated linear and tree ensemble models, and dynamically deployed the optimal ROC-AUC model.


================================================================================
SLIDE 2: DATA UNDERSTANDING & FEATURE ENGINEERING
================================================================================
* Aggregated Historical Totals: Summed rep calls, samples provided, digital engagements, competitive Rx, and medical events across Q1–Q10 to capture cumulative engagement intensity.
* Temporal Windows (Recency vs. Early):
  - Early Window (Q1–Q3): Established initial baseline engagement levels.
  - Recency Window (Q8–Q10): Captured late-stage physician behavior and recent event participation.
* Dynamic Trend Features: Differences between recency and early metrics (recency_* - early_*) to quantify growing or declining HCP interest over time.
* Behavioral Momentum Indicator: Binary flag for strictly monotonic non-decreasing rep calls in late quarters (Q7–Q10).


================================================================================
SLIDE 3: PREPROCESSING & DATA LEAKAGE SAFEGUARDS
================================================================================
* Train/Validation Split: 80/20 stratified split applied on the non-test training pool prior to fitting any transformers.
* Missing Value Imputation: Numerical missing values imputed strictly using training set medians (X_train.median()).
* Territory Target Encoding: Territory-level adoption rates and average rep calls calculated exclusively on X_train and mapped to validation and test sets with global mean fallback.
* Unsupervised Clustering: 5-cluster K-Means built on scaled engagement metrics to group physician behavior profiles.
* Multicollinearity Elimination: Variance Inflation Factor (VIF) filtering with a threshold of 10.0 applied strictly to numeric features to prevent instability in linear models.


================================================================================
SLIDE 4: MODEL BUILDING JOURNEY
================================================================================
* Iterative Modeling Strategy: Evaluated three distinct algorithms (Logistic Regression, Random Forest, and XGBoost) to compare linear baselines against non-linear tree ensembles.
* Logistic Regression: Standard baseline using L2 regularization on standard-scaled and VIF-filtered features.
* Random Forest Classifier: 200 estimators, max depth of 8, minimum sample leaf of 5; out-of-bag (OOB) scoring evaluated for generalization.
* XGBoost Hyperparameter Tuning: Automated 15-trial Optuna optimization using 5-Fold Stratified Cross-Validation on X_train with target ROC-AUC metric.
* Search Space Expansion: Tuned max_depth (4–9), n_estimators (50–200), and learning_rate (0.01–0.1 log-scale).


