================================================================================
SLIDE 6: KEY DRIVERS OF ADOPTION
================================================================================
* Top Predictive Features:
  - Competitive Rx Volume (total_competitive_rx): High existing category volume serves as the strongest baseline indicator of potential adoption.
  - Rep Call Recency & Trend (recency_rep_calls, trend_rep_calls): Recent sales push and positive call momentum strongly correlate with adoption probability.
  - Peer Network & Event Engagement (avg_peer_network_score, speaker_recency_q8_q10): High peer influence and recent speaker program attendance significantly boost conversion likelihood.
* Model Interpretability: Combined standard coefficient magnitudes from Logistic Regression with Gini/Gain feature importances from Random Forest and XGBoost to validate key business drivers across model architectures.


================================================================================
SLIDE 7: ESTIMATED ADOPTION PROBABILITIES & TOP-200 TARGET SUMMARY
================================================================================
* Test Set Inference: Predicted adoption probabilities across all 1,502 unseen test physicians (test_physicians.csv) using historical Q1–Q10 features.
* Top-200 Selection Strategy: Sorted test physicians by predicted probability in descending order and assigned binary target flags (top_200_target_flag = 1).
* Probability Distribution Summary:
  - Top 200 Average Adoption Probability: Evaluated high probability concentration among top targets.
  - Top 200 Minimum Cutoff Threshold: Minimum probability score required to enter the top-200 targeting tier.
* Outputs Generated: Full prediction file exported to predictions.csv and high-priority targets exported to top_200_targets_q11.xlsx.


